      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nstatic long long modPow(long long base, long long exponent) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    while (exponent > 0) {\n        if (exponent & 1LL) result = result * base % MOD;\n        base = base * base % MOD;\n        exponent >>= 1LL;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nclass Binomial {\npublic:\n    explicit Binomial(int maxN) : fact(maxN + 1), invFact(maxN + 1) {\n        fact[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= maxN; ++i) fact[i] = fact[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n        invFact[maxN] = modPow(fact[maxN], MOD - 2);\n        for (int i = maxN; i > 0; --i) invFact[i - 1] = invFact[i] * i % MOD;\n    }\n\n    long long choose(int n, int k) const {\n        if (k < 0 || k > n) return 0;\n        return fact[n] * invFact[k] % MOD * invFact[n - k] % MOD;\n    }\n\nprivate:\n    vector<long long> fact;\n    vector<long long> invFact;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<pair<int, int> > obstacles;\n    obstacles.reserve(m);\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int row, col;\n        cin >> row >> col;\n        obstacles.push_back(make_pair(row, col));\n    }\n\n    sort(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end());\n    obstacles.erase(unique(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end()), obstacles.end());\n\n    if (!obstacles.empty() &&\n        ((obstacles.front().first == 0 && obstacles.front().second == 0) ||\n         (obstacles.back().first == n - 1 && obstacles.back().second == n - 1))) {\n        cout << 0 << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    // Use obstacle-pair work only while it is well below the dense grid scan.\n    if (obstacles.size() <= static_cast<size_t>(n / 4)) {\n        Binomial binomial(2 * n - 2);\n        sort(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end(),\n             [](const pair<int, int>& left, const pair<int, int>& right) {\n                 const int leftDiagonal = left.first + left.second;\n                 const int rightDiagonal = right.first + right.second;\n                 if (leftDiagonal != rightDiagonal) return leftDiagonal < rightDiagonal;\n                 return left < right;\n             });\n\n        vector<long long> firstHit(obstacles.size(), 0);\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < obstacles.size(); ++i) {\n            const int row = obstacles[i].first;\n            const int col = obstacles[i].second;\n            long long ways = binomial.choose(row + col, row);\n\n            for (size_t j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n                const int previousRow = obstacles[j].first;\n                const int previousCol = obstacles[j].second;\n                if (previousRow <= row && previousCol <= col) {\n                    const int rowDelta = row - previousRow;\n                    const int colDelta = col - previousCol;\n                    const long long throughPrevious =\n                        firstHit[j] * binomial.choose(rowDelta + colDelta, rowDelta) % MOD;\n                    ways -= throughPrevious;\n                    if (ways < 0) ways += MOD;\n                }\n            }\n            firstHit[i] = ways;\n        }\n\n        long long answer = binomial.choose(2 * n - 2, n - 1);\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < obstacles.size(); ++i) {\n            const int remainingRows = n - 1 - obstacles[i].first;\n            const int remainingCols = n - 1 - obstacles[i].second;\n            const long long throughObstacle =\n                firstHit[i] * binomial.choose(remainingRows + remainingCols, remainingRows) % MOD;\n            answer -= throughObstacle;\n            if (answer < 0) answer += MOD;\n        }\n\n        cout << answer << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    // Dense fallback: one contiguous row holds the values from the previous row\n    // and is updated in place from left to right.\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    size_t obstacleIndex = 0;\n    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n        for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n            if (obstacleIndex < obstacles.size() &&\n                obstacles[obstacleIndex].first == row &&\n                obstacles[obstacleIndex].second == col) {\n                dp[col] = 0;\n                ++obstacleIndex;\n            } else if (row == 0 && col == 0) {\n                dp[col] = 1;\n            } else if (col > 0) {\n                int value = dp[col] + dp[col - 1];\n                if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n                dp[col] = value;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "A work-based hybrid should improve locality and avoid unnecessary dense-grid work: sparse obstacle coordinates use diagonal-order combinatorial counting, while denser cases use a contiguous, in-place row-major DP row instead of an N×N blocked bitmap and per-row copying.",
  "notes": "This source handles duplicate obstacles and blocked endpoints explicitly; the dense fallback preserves exact DP behavior. No commands or tests were run.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Store blocked coordinates as a deduplicated O(M) vector and use first-hit binomial path counts when the obstacle-pair work is below a conservative N-based crossover.",
    "For denser cases, scan obstacles in row-major order alongside a single contiguous DP row, update it in place, and replace modulo operations with conditional reductions."
